---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Navbar from "../../components/Navbar.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of Use | RIP Wallet"
  description="Terms of Use for Tabs, the personal finance tracking app by RIP Wallet."
>
  <Navbar currentPath="/legal/terms" />

  <header class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 pt-24 pb-12 animate-reveal">
    <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-yellow-600 mb-4">
      Tabs · Legal
    </p>
    <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-4">
      Terms of Use
    </h1>
    <div class="flex items-center gap-3 text-sm text-gray-500 font-mono">
      <span>Last updated July 7, 2026</span>
      <span class="text-gray-300">·</span>
      <span>RIP Wallet</span>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-gray-500 italic leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
      By downloading, installing, or using Tabs, you agree to these terms.
      <strong class="not-italic text-gray-900">Tabs is a calculator, not a financial advisor</strong>
      — read section 2 before making decisions based on its numbers.
    </p>
  </header>

  <main class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 pb-32">
    <nav class="bg-white border border-gray-100 rounded-2xl p-6 shadow-sm mb-12 animate-reveal delay-1">
      <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-gray-400 mb-4">On this page</p>
      <ol class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-2 list-none p-0 m-0">
        <li><a href="#service" class="legal-toc-link"><span class="legal-toc-n">01</span>Description of the service</a></li>
        <li><a href="#not-advice" class="legal-toc-link"><span class="legal-toc-n">02</span>Not financial advice</a></li>
        <li><a href="#eligibility" class="legal-toc-link"><span class="legal-toc-n">03</span>Eligibility</a></li>
        <li><a href="#license" class="legal-toc-link"><span class="legal-toc-n">04</span>License to use</a></li>
        <li><a href="#your-data" class="legal-toc-link"><span class="legal-toc-n">05</span>Your data</a></li>
        <li><a href="#purchases" class="legal-toc-link"><span class="legal-toc-n">06</span>In-app purchases</a></li>
        <li><a href="#prohibited" class="legal-toc-link"><span class="legal-toc-n">07</span>Prohibited uses</a></li>
        <li><a href="#warranties" class="legal-toc-link"><span class="legal-toc-n">08</span>Disclaimer of warranties</a></li>
        <li><a href="#liability" class="legal-toc-link"><span class="legal-toc-n">09</span>Limitation of liability</a></li>
        <li><a href="#termination" class="legal-toc-link"><span class="legal-toc-n">10</span>Termination</a></li>
        <li><a href="#changes" class="legal-toc-link"><span class="legal-toc-n">11</span>Changes to these terms</a></li>
        <li><a href="#law" class="legal-toc-link"><span class="legal-toc-n">12</span>Governing law</a></li>
        <li><a href="#contact" class="legal-toc-link"><span class="legal-toc-n">13</span>Contact us</a></li>
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <hr class="border-t border-gray-100 my-10" />

    <section id="service" class="legal-section">
      <p class="legal-n">01</p>
      <h2 class="legal-h2">Description of the service</h2>
      <p>Tabs is a personal finance tracking tool that helps you record and estimate:</p>
      <ul class="legal-list">
        <li>Debts (loans, credit cards, etc.) and their projected payoff timeline based on the interest rate, term, and payments you enter</li>
        <li>Investments, savings, and other assets, along with their return on investment</li>
        <li>Your overall net worth over time, calculated from the figures you enter</li>
      </ul>
      <p>All calculations are performed locally on your device, based entirely on the data you provide.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="not-advice" class="legal-section">
      <p class="legal-n">02</p>
      <h2 class="legal-h2">Not financial advice</h2>
      <div class="legal-callout">
        <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-yellow-600 mb-2">Read this before you rely on the numbers</p>
        <p class="m-0"><strong>Tabs is a calculator and tracking tool — it is not a financial advisor, and nothing in the App constitutes financial, investment, tax, or legal advice.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <ul class="legal-list">
        <li>Payoff dates, interest projections, and "what-if" scenarios are estimates based solely on the numbers you enter. They assume steady, uninterrupted behavior (e.g. consistent payments) and do not account for real-world changes such as rate adjustments, fees, market volatility, or missed payments unless you update your entries accordingly.</li>
        <li>Currency conversions use live exchange rates that fluctuate and may not exactly match the rate you receive from your bank or broker.</li>
        <li>You are solely responsible for verifying the accuracy of any figures you enter and for any financial decisions you make. Consult a qualified financial professional before making significant financial decisions.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="eligibility" class="legal-section">
      <p class="legal-n">03</p>
      <h2 class="legal-h2">Eligibility</h2>
      <p>You must be able to form a binding contract to use the App. If you are using the App on behalf of a minor or with a shared household device, you are responsible for ensuring appropriate use.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="license" class="legal-section">
      <p class="legal-n">04</p>
      <h2 class="legal-h2">License to use</h2>
      <p>We grant you a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable license to download and use the App on devices you own or control, solely for your personal, non-commercial use, subject to these Terms.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="your-data" class="legal-section">
      <p class="legal-n">05</p>
      <h2 class="legal-h2">Your data</h2>
      <p>All data you enter into the App is stored locally on your device. You are solely responsible for:</p>
      <ul class="legal-list">
        <li>The accuracy of the information you enter</li>
        <li>Backing up your data if desired (e.g. via the App's CSV export feature)</li>
        <li>Any consequences of losing your data if you uninstall the App, lose your device, or otherwise lose access to it, since we do not maintain a copy</li>
      </ul>
      <p>See our <a href="/legal/privacy" class="text-yellow-600 underline underline-offset-2 hover:opacity-75">Privacy Policy</a> for details on how your data is (and is not) handled.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="purchases" class="legal-section">
      <p class="legal-n">06</p>
      <h2 class="legal-h2">In-app purchases</h2>
      <p>Tabs offers an optional one-time purchase ("Tabs Pro") that unlocks additional features. This is a <strong>single, non-recurring payment — there is no subscription and no recurring charge.</strong></p>
      <ul class="legal-list">
        <li>Purchases are processed entirely through the Apple App Store or Google Play Store, and are subject to their respective terms and refund policies. We do not process payments ourselves and cannot directly issue refunds — refund requests must go through Apple or Google.</li>
        <li>Features included in the free tier and in Tabs Pro may change over time as the App evolves, but any purchase you've already made will continue to unlock the Pro features active at the time of your purchase.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="prohibited" class="legal-section">
      <p class="legal-n">07</p>
      <h2 class="legal-h2">Prohibited uses</h2>
      <p>You agree not to:</p>
      <ul class="legal-list">
        <li>Reverse-engineer, decompile, or attempt to extract the source code of the App, except where applicable law expressly permits it</li>
        <li>Use the App for any unlawful purpose</li>
        <li>Attempt to interfere with, disrupt, or gain unauthorized access to any systems related to the App</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="warranties" class="legal-section">
      <p class="legal-n">08</p>
      <h2 class="legal-h2">Disclaimer of warranties</h2>
      <p>The App is provided <strong>"as is" and "as available," without warranties of any kind</strong>, whether express or implied, including but not limited to implied warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and non-infringement. We do not warrant that the App will be uninterrupted, error-free, or that calculations will be accurate for your specific financial situation.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="liability" class="legal-section">
      <p class="legal-n">09</p>
      <h2 class="legal-h2">Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>To the fullest extent permitted by law, RIP Wallet shall not be liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages, or any loss of data, profits, or financial loss, arising out of or related to your use of (or inability to use) the App, including any financial decisions made based on information calculated or displayed by the App.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="termination" class="legal-section">
      <p class="legal-n">10</p>
      <h2 class="legal-h2">Termination</h2>
      <p>You may stop using the App at any time by uninstalling it. We reserve the right to suspend or discontinue the App, or any features within it, at any time.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="changes" class="legal-section">
      <p class="legal-n">11</p>
      <h2 class="legal-h2">Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p>We may update these Terms from time to time. If we make material changes, we will update the "Last updated" date above. Continued use of the App after changes take effect constitutes acceptance of the revised Terms.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="law" class="legal-section">
      <p class="legal-n">12</p>
      <h2 class="legal-h2">Governing law</h2>
      <p>These Terms are governed by the laws of Costa Rica, without regard to its conflict-of-law principles, except where local consumer protection laws in your jurisdiction require otherwise.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="contact" class="legal-section">
      <p class="legal-n">13</p>
      <h2 class="legal-h2">Contact us</h2>
      <p>If you have any questions about these Terms, reach out any time — we read every message.</p>
      <div class="mt-8 p-6 bg-white border border-gray-100 rounded-2xl shadow-sm flex flex-wrap justify-between items-center gap-4">
        <div>
          <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-gray-400 mb-1">Questions about these terms</p>
          <p class="text-lg font-bold m-0">RIP Wallet</p>
        </div>
        <a href="mailto:hola@spentapp.co" class="font-mono text-sm text-yellow-600 underline underline-offset-2 hover:opacity-75">hola@spentapp.co</a>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-4 font-mono text-sm text-gray-500">
        Also see the <a href="/legal/privacy" class="text-yellow-600 underline underline-offset-2 hover:opacity-75">Privacy Policy</a> for Tabs.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style is:global>
  .legal-section {
    margin-top: 48px;
    scroll-margin-top: 80px;
  }
  .legal-n {
    font-family: ui-monospace, monospace;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: #ca8a04;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }
  .legal-h2 {
    font-size: 22px;
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.2;
    margin: 4px 0 0;
    color: #111827;
  }
  .legal-section p {
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: #374151;
    margin: 14px 0;
    max-width: 66ch;
  }
  .legal-list {
    margin: 14px 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    max-width: 64ch;
  }
  .legal-list li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 22px;
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin: 9px 0;
    color: #374151;
  }
  .legal-list li::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.65em;
    width: 7px;
    height: 7px;
    background: #facc15;
    border-radius: 1px;
    transform: rotate(45deg);
  }
  .legal-callout {
    margin: 20px 0;
    padding: 18px 20px;
    background: #ffffff;
    border: 1px solid #f3f4f6;
    border-left: 3px solid #facc15;
    border-radius: 10px;
    box-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,0.04), 0 4px 12px rgba(0,0,0,0.03);
  }
  .legal-callout p {
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: #374151;
  }
  .legal-toc-link {
    display: flex;
    gap: 10px;
    align-items: baseline;
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 14px;
    color: #111827;
    text-decoration: none;
    padding: 3px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid transparent;
    transition: border-color 0.15s ease, color 0.15s ease;
  }
  .legal-toc-link:hover {
    color: #ca8a04;
    border-bottom-color: #ca8a04;
  }
  .legal-toc-n {
    font-family: ui-monospace, monospace;
    font-size: 12px;
    color: #9ca3af;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    flex: none;
  }
  .legal-toc-link:hover .legal-toc-n {
    color: #ca8a04;
  }

  @keyframes reveal {
    from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(10px); }
    to { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); }
  }
  .animate-reveal {
    opacity: 0;
    animation: reveal 0.8s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1) forwards;
  }
  .delay-1 { animation-delay: 0.1s; }
</style>
